# Operator consistency

Meat Bags operate this at a desk. One job has one name. That name is the same on buttons, copied URLs, HTTP paths, event `action`, status lines, tray copy, and docs.

You already know whether two words mean the same thing. If they do, pick the one already in use and drop the other. If they do not, they must not sit on the same surface as if they were opposites.

Do not maintain a synonym list in this file. `docs/SPEC.md` is the product. Read the live chrome and match it. Adding a third word for an existing job is a bug. Mixing two families on one control (Show all as the reverse of Stop all) is a bug. A label that changes family by state is a bug.

When you rename, rename the whole family in one pass: UI, routes, events, overlay messages, tests, pages. Alpha: no leftover aliases.

Internal helpers may keep boring names. Anything a Meat Bag reads or pastes must agree with itself.
